# Where the tarball beside this file came from — and why a tarball this stack never installs is
# vendored at all.
#
# THE AIO BAKE NEEDS IT. AIO's entrypoint installs notify_push on every start (Containers/nextcloud/
# entrypoint.sh:726-733) and the notify-push container exits 1 without the binary (Containers/
# notify-push/start.sh:31-42). With the store off in this suite (patch 020), first boot fails unless
# the bake carries the app — and the bake needs bytes with provenance: vendoring survives an
# offline install (#98), a store that moved (#163), and D7's no-source-fork rule.
#
# THIS STACK DOES NOT INSTALL IT: notify_push is in NO inventory (APPS, OWN_APPS). gestion's
# compose stack runs no push server; the tarball exists so the AIO bake can copy it in. The
# static gates still hold it to every rule — exactly one tarball, name id-version.tar.gz, sha256
# matching, a LICENSING row — because both glob provisioning/apps/*/ without asking any inventory.
#
# The version is the newest NC34-compatible store release, resolved via the platform index
# (https://apps.nextcloud.com/api/v1/platform/34.0.0/apps.json — scripts/app-versions.sh's INDEX,
# same scoping rule: platform-scoped already means "runs on the NC this suite pins").
